{"id": "unknown-2026-10-06-005", "date": "2026-10-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Wireless bipolar electrodes raise zinc-air battery power by 80%", "content": "<p>Researchers in Spain and Argentina have developed a zinc-air battery architecture that increases power output by up to 80% by reducing internal resistance without changing the device’s core chemistry. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/06/wireless-bipolar-electrodes-raise-zinc-air-battery-power-by-80/\">Wireless bipolar electrodes raise zinc-air battery power by 80%</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/06/wireless-bipolar-electrodes-raise-zinc-air-battery-power-by-80/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-06-006", "date": "2026-10-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["trade_tariff", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Japan proposes four categories for priority commercial solar support", "content": "<p>Japan wants to prioritize future subsidies for new commercial solar projects it considers compatible with local communities, as ground-mounted plants lose feed-in tariff (FIT) and feed-in premium (FIP) support from April 2027.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/06/japan-proposes-four-categories-for-priority-commercial-solar-support/\">Japan proposes four categories for priority commercial solar support</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv mag", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/06/japan-proposes-four-categories-for-priority-commercial-solar-support/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-06-007", "date": "2026-10-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Poland unveils new home storage subsidy", "content": "<p>Poland's latest subsidy scheme will offer existing prosumers support to purchase and install home storage units. The PLN 1 billion ($258 million) funding call opens for applications on October 20.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/06/poland-unveils-new-home-storage-subsidy/\">Poland unveils new home storage subsidy </a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/06/poland-unveils-new-home-storage-subsidy/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-06-008", "date": "2026-10-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Heliene launches all-black solar module for residential rooftops", "content": "<p>The North American module manufacturer has introduced its 108HC M10 SL All-Black residential solar panel, offering power outputs up to 410 W and 21.0% efficiency built on a 108 half-cut cell architecture.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/06/heliene-launches-108hc-m10-sl-all-black-solar-module-for-residential-rooftops/\">Heliene launches all-black solar module for residential rooftops</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/06/heliene-launches-108hc-m10-sl-all-black-solar-module-for-residential-rooftops/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-06-009", "date": "2026-10-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Spacebound silicon", "content": "<p>Solar has a long history in powering satellites and space exploration, and high-powered devices based on multijunction PV cells made from “III-V” materials such as gallium arsenide or indium gallium phosphide have supplied this niche market as far back as the 1960s. But those devices are made with rare materials and complex processing, limited to small batches produced at high cost.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/06/spacebound-silicon/\">Spacebound silicon</a> app", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/06/spacebound-silicon/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-06-010", "date": "2026-10-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Indian startup claims over 1,500 cycles for sodium-ion cell with Prussian white cathode", "content": "<p>Indian startup Macsen Energy claims its Prussian white-based sodium-ion battery cell has exceeded 1,500 charge-discharge cycles in laboratory testing, retaining 90% of its initial capacity after 1,000 cycles. The company also plans to build a cathode material production facility and battery cell pilot line, with construction set to begin in 2027. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/06/indian-startup-claims-over-1500-cycles-for-sodium-ion-cell-with-prussian-white-cath", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/06/indian-startup-claims-over-1500-cycles-for-sodium-ion-cell-with-prussian-white-cathode/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-06-011", "date": "2026-10-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["installation_demand", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Thailand tightens solar panel safety standards", "content": "<p>Thailand will now require crystalline silicon solar panels to meet national safety standards in its latest effort to improve the quality and safety of solar installations.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/06/thailand-tightens-solar-panel-safety-standards/\">Thailand tightens solar panel safety standards</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/06/thailand-tightens-solar-panel-safety-standards/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-06-012", "date": "2026-10-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "What’s driving Europe’s battery boom? Insights from EUPD Research’s Business Climate Survey and Storage Report", "content": "<p>Europe’s battery storage market is projected to nearly double from 34 GWh in 2025 to 65 GWh in 2026, driven primarily by utility-scale projects and growing renewable energy integration.<br />\nMeanwhile, intensifying competition in residential and commercial storage is pushing manufacturers toward integrated energy solutions, strategic partnerships, and advanced energy management technologies.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/06/whats-driving-europes-battery-boom-in", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/06/whats-driving-europes-battery-boom-insights-from-eupd-researchs-business-climate-survey-and-storage-report/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-06-013", "date": "2026-10-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Building quality domestic U.S. cell fabs is more important than technology-choice today", "content": "Analysis taken from the new Solar Manufacturing USA Quarterly report highlights steady progress with c-Si cell production during 2026, with strong upside to the forecast through 2027 if existing lines can be ramped effectively and some of the 2027 plans are brought forward by just a few months.", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine_usa", "url": "https://pv-magazine-usa.com/2026/10/06/building-quality-domestic-u-s-cell-fabs-is-more-important-than-technology-choice-today/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-06-014", "date": "2026-10-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Inside the six-week commissioning of a 160 MW Texas battery", "content": "U.S. controls provider FlexGen says catching faults in its lab before crews reach site, then scripting the grid tests, got a Houston battery into the Electric Reliability Council of Texas (ERCOT) market this summer far inside the 25 weeks or more it considers typical.", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine_usa", "url": "https://pv-magazine-usa.com/2026/10/06/inside-the-six-week-commissioning-of-a-160-mw-texas-battery/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-06-015", "date": "2026-10-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "New research quantifies local economic impact of rural wind and solar buildout", "content": "A nationwide study by the Center for Rural Energy Security at the University of Missouri reveals that utility-scale wind projects deliver substantial, lasting boosts to county-level GDP, while solar developments generate more localized gains concentrated primarily in construction and utilities. ", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine_usa", "url": "https://pv-magazine-usa.com/2026/10/06/new-research-quantifies-local-economic-impact-of-rural-wind-and-solar-buildout/", "type": "rss"}]}
