{"id": "unknown-2026-10-06-017", "date": "2026-10-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "This funky solar electric scooter could handle your commute without ever plugging in", "content": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://electrek.co/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/10/lightfoot-solar-scooter-head.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">There are plenty of ways to build a small electric vehicle. These days, the prevailing options have been to make it faster, give it more power, slap on bigger tires, or keep adding features until your humble little scooter has somehow turned into a 150-pound electric motorcycle.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-b", "sources": [{"name": "electrek_solar", "url": "https://electrek.co/2026/10/06/this-funky-solar-electric-scooter-could-handle-your-commute-without-ever-plugging-in/", "type": "rss"}]}
